      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Agreed. I don't want the clutter on my desktop mode UI. I don't want a hamburger icon on the top left and a second microphone icon on the top right. The only way to truly remove them is to set the HUD transparency to max, but then you can't see the mic icon anymore, or any notifications like invites, friend requests, group announcements, etc...\n\nIt's incredibly distracting. It's hindered my experience so much that I actually cancelled my VRC+ and I will not be giving another cent to VRChat until this change is reverted, and I have given a considerable amount already with the intention of giving more. I wanted to support a platform I believed in, but I'm realizing that was a mistake and VRChat is no longer what it once was. Looking at the Steam discussions, there are others who feel the same way and have cancelled their subscriptions as well.\n\nI have a Steam Index, and yet I choose to play on Desktop mode for the majority of my time on VRChat. I'd say over 3000 hours of my time on VRChat has been on Desktop mode. It's just easier to hop in for a bit, hang out with people, and I don't got to wear a headset all day. I'm not always able to commit to an entire day of having a headset on my face as life can call me away from my computer at any time. I usually reserve my headset for more special or coordinated occasions. Desktop mode is good enough without all the changes, and everything was already pretty straight forward. Having to remind me that there's a menu that I could access by pressing Escape by permanently burning a hamburger menu onto the top left of the screen is incredibly insulting. To me, it tells me you guys just don't care, especially after you received a ton of feedback from beta testers saying that it was a bad idea.\n\nPlease, at the very least, allow us to turn off the new on screen elements completely. There already is an option to turn it down to minimal... please just add that one extra step. Please. And also make it remove the \"Press Alt + H to hide the HUD\" part when you press escape too.\n\nThat's all. That's all I'm asking for. That's all everyone is asking for.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
